meta {
  name: Daily Agenda (/agenda)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/agenda
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
}

vars:post-response {
  firstAgendaPatientId: res.body && res.body.rows && res.body.rows.length ? res.body.rows[0].patientId : ''
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.rows: isArray
}

docs {
  UC-6 (REQUIREMENTS.md): the day's not-yet-seen roster for the launched clinician, one safety-flagged
  summary row per patient (ARCHITECTURE.md §19). Requires an AgendaSessionContext, which only a real
  `/agenda/launch` browser login can create - see this collection's README ("Getting a session
  cookie") for how to obtain one and put it in the `local` environment's `sessionCookie` variable.
  With no session, AgendaEndpoints.HandleGetAgendaAsync returns 401 before it ever calls OpenEMR, so
  the assertions above fail closed rather than reporting green with nothing behind them.

  Captures the roster's first patientId into `firstAgendaPatientId` (empty string if the roster came
  back empty, e.g. a 401 body or a day with nothing left) for Select Patient.bru, run next.
}
